{"content":[{"c":["GOIIM"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. People or region mentioned in ",{"href":"?bref=Gen.14.1,9","r":"Gen.14.1,9","rawR":"Gen.14.1,9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.14.1,9","value":"Gen.14.1,9"}],"t":"ref","v":"Genesis 14:1, 9"}," as ruled by a king named Tidal. The word is variously translated “nations” (",{"c":["kjv"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"},") and “Goiim” (",{"c":["rsv"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"},", ",{"c":["nlt"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"},"). Tidal, together with three other kings—Amraphel of Shinar, Arioch of Ellasar, and Kedorlaomer of Elam—attacked several cities in the valley of Siddim near the Dead Sea (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.14.3","r":"Gen.14.3","rawR":"Gen.14.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.14.3","value":"Gen.14.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 14:3"},"). They defeated the five kings of the valley region, looted their towns, and captured Lot, Abraham’s nephew, who lived in Sodom (v ",{"href":"?bref=Gen.14.12","r":"Gen.14.12","rawR":"Gen.14.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.14.12","value":"Gen.14.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"12"},"). When Abraham heard of this, he gathered his soldiers, pursued the victorious kings, defeated them, and rescued Lot (vv ",{"href":"?bref=Gen.14.13-16","r":"Gen.14.13-16","rawR":"Gen.14.13-16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.14.13-16","value":"Gen.14.13-16"}],"t":"ref","v":"13-16"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. People mentioned in connection with Joshua’s victory over an unknown king of Goiim (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.12.23","r":"Josh.12.23","rawR":"Josh.12.23","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.12.23","value":"Josh.12.23"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 12:23"},"). The location of these people is uncertain, since the verse reads “Gilgal” in the Hebrew text and “Galilee” in the Septuagint."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Goiim","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Genesis 14:1, 9","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.14.1,9","rawQueryValue":"Gen.14.1,9","sourceRefExact":"Gen.14.1,9"},{"anchorText":"Gn 14:3","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.14.3","rawQueryValue":"Gen.14.3","sourceRefExact":"Gen.14.3"},{"anchorText":"12","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.14.12","rawQueryValue":"Gen.14.12","sourceRefExact":"Gen.14.12"},{"anchorText":"13-16","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.14.13-16","rawQueryValue":"Gen.14.13-16","sourceRefExact":"Gen.14.13-16"},{"anchorText":"Jos 12:23","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.12.23","rawQueryValue":"Josh.12.23","sourceRefExact":"Josh.12.23"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"de000de6f570a33cdd85a2e39d89852ce513ad3fd0caf2f08897a2f6063d974f","sourceItemName":"Goiim","sourceItemOrder":177,"sourceMember":"Articles/G.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Goiim","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Goiim","title":"Goiim","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}